  },
  "content": {
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "order": 1,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "text": "Six children were in the hospital."
          },
          {
            "id": "s2",
            "text": "They were very sick, but the doctors didn’t know what to do."
          },
          {
            "id": "s3",
            "text": "They called Dr. Richard Besser, an expert on strange illnesses."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "order": 2,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s4",
            "text": "First, Dr. Besser needed to find the cause of the illness."
          },
          {
            "id": "s5",
            "text": "He looked for germs in the children’s bodies."
          },
          {
            "id": "s6",
            "text": "In every child, Dr. Besser found the same type of the bacteria E. coli."
          },
          {
            "id": "s7",
            "text": "He then looked at the bacteria’s DNA."
          },
          {
            "id": "s8",
            "text": "2 It showed him that this type of E. coli was dangerous."
          },
          {
            "id": "s9",
            "text": "2 DNA is a chemical that contains information about a living thing’s characteristics."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "order": 3,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s10",
            "text": "Dr. Besser knew E. coli could move from animals to humans."
          },
          {
            "id": "s11",
            "text": "Had the children touched animals that carried the bacteria?"
          },
          {
            "id": "s12",
            "text": "Besser found other E. coli cases in the area where the children lived."
          },
          {
            "id": "s13",
            "text": "But it wasn’t enough."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "order": 4,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s14",
            "text": "Besser then made a list of what the sick children had eaten."
          },
          {
            "id": "s15",
            "text": "They had all eaten cheese, apple juice, and fish."
          },
          {
            "id": "s16",
            "text": "He then made a list of what healthy children in the area had eaten."
          },
          {
            "id": "s17",
            "text": "They had eaten the cheese and fish, but not the apple juice."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "order": 5,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s18",
            "text": "Besser went to where the apple juice was made."
          },
          {
            "id": "s19",
            "text": "He saw animals around the apple trees."
          },
          {
            "id": "s20",
            "text": "He also saw the workers using dirty apples that had fallen on the ground."
          },
          {
            "id": "s21",
            "text": "More importantly, he saw that the apples were not washed before the juice was made, and that the juice was not heated."
          },
          {
            "id": "s22",
            "text": "Doing these things would kill the bacteria."
          },
          {
            "id": "s23",
            "text": "Besser then knew it was the apple juice that made the children sick."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "order": 6,
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "s24",
            "text": "Besser’s E. coli case had a happy ending."
          },
          {
            "id": "s25",
            "text": "The children got better."
          },
          {
            "id": "s26",
            "text": "And what Besser learned that day now helps keep others safe."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
